  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Monday)\nIssued at 208 PM CDT TUE JUL 28 2026\n\nOur area will remain in a northwest flow upper level pattern, on\nthe eastern periphery of the big heat dome, through most of the\nrest of the work week. Weak disturbances in this flow regime could\nhelp kick off isolated/scattered showers and storms during this\ntime. With the center of the upper high moving back to the west, \nafternoon temperatures the next few days should moderate some back\ndown to more \"typical\" summertime levels. While the southern \ncounties in our CWA may be close to Heat Advisory criteria, I \ndon't think the confidence criteria exceedance is high enough to \nwarrant an extension of the Advisory at this time.\n\nAs we transition to the weekend, the computer models are\nadvertising a much more substantial shortwave trough digging into\nthe southeast states from the north. This trough will further\n\"cool\" temperatures, and bring an enhanced chance of showers and \nstorms to our area Saturday and Sunday. Beyond the weekend, it\nlooks like that upper low just hangs around into at least early\nnext week, keeping temperatures manageable and keeping rain\nchances a bit elevated.\n\n/61/",
